\tag{acceptance-test}
\tag{area:fd}
\tag{status:proposed}

\p{State the Lean universes of the root, labelled shapes, matrix families, walking structures, monad collection, \code{Mod}, and projected category API. Check the intended matrix signature from \ref{dec-rt-0027} and the individual entry/collection levels. Compile examples with object/entry levels \code{(0,1)}, \code{(1,1)}, and \code{(1,0)}, plus the intended \code{Set}, small-space, and category collections. Provide necessary lifts and prove their comparison lemmas; no universe-lowering axiom is allowed.}
\p{\strong{Depends on:} \ref{ms-0000} toolchain; minimal types only. \strong{Evidence:} actual declarations, compiled examples, universe table. \strong{Failure response:} increase collection universes or separate parameters; do not weaken the category API by silently forcing \code{u=v}.}
\p{Named by: \ref{dec-ch-0023}, \ref{dec-fd-0001}, \ref{dec-rt-0025}, \ref{dec-rt-0027}, \ref{dec-sp-0010}.}
\p{\em{Partial Lean declarations:} \code{Prototype.Universes.Matrix}, its \code{Map}, \code{liftEntries}, \code{liftMap}, and \code{lowerMap} operations, and the seven laws in \code{Prototype/Universes/Matrix.lean}. Explicit matrix universe examples and theorem axiom reports are in \code{Prototype/Universes/Examples.lean}.}
\p{\em{Object-label comparisons:} \code{Prototype/Universes/Reindex.lean} defines \code{reindex}, \code{reindexMap}, \code{liftLabels}, \code{lowerLabels}, \code{liftLabelsMap}, and \code{lowerLabelsMap} in the same matrix namespace, with twelve laws for reindexing, inverse comparisons, and commutation with entry lifting. The examples include all three object/entry orderings and a mixed lift at four distinct levels.}
\p{\em{Evidence and scope:} \code{Prototype/Universes/README.md} records the universe table and validation results. This covers matrix families, reindexing, and object/entry lifts; the remaining root, shape, walking, monad, \code{Mod}, space, and category signatures and necessary comparisons are still outstanding. The complete statement is unchanged at version 1 and remains proposed.}
